The error log indicates that the devicetree node for `zephyr,adc-emul` instance 0 cannot be found. This is because the C code uses `DT_INST(0, zephyr_adc_emul)` to get the device node, but no node in the devicetree is configured with `compatible = "zephyr,adc-emul"` and `status = "okay"`.

The test overlay file `tests/drivers/adc/adc_emul/app.overlay` modifies the `&adc0` node but does not set its compatible property or status. To fix this, we need to explicitly set the compatible to `"zephyr,adc-emul"` and the status to `"okay"` for the `adc0` node within the overlay file. This will ensure that the devicetree macros can correctly identify and access the emulated ADC device instance.

tests/drivers/adc/adc_emul/app.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
&adc0 {
	ref-internal-mv = <3300>;
	ref-external1-mv = <5000>;
};
========
&adc0 {
	compatible = "zephyr,adc-emul";
	status = "okay";
	ref-internal-mv = <3300>;
	ref-external1-mv = <5000>;
};
>>>>>>>> REPLACE

The Kconfig warning indicates that the `CONFIG_ADC_EMUL` option is being disabled because its dependency on `DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_ADC_EMUL_ENABLED` is not met. This dependency requires an enabled devicetree node with `compatible = "zephyr,adc-emul"`.

The provided `app.overlay` file attempts to modify an existing `&adc0` node. This approach fails on platforms that do not have a pre-existing `adc0` node or alias, which is common for emulation targets. As a result, the devicetree node for the ADC emulator is not created, causing the Kconfig dependency to fail.

The subsequent linker errors are a direct result of this configuration issue. With `CONFIG_ADC_EMUL` disabled, the ADC emulator driver is not compiled, leading to undefined references to its API functions (e.g., `adc_emul_const_value_set`). The `undefined reference to '__device_dts_ord_1'` error also stems from the missing devicetree node, as the `DEVICE_DT_GET` macro cannot find the device.

To fix this, the overlay file should be modified to unconditionally define a new node for the ADC emulator, rather than attempting to modify a potentially non-existent one. This ensures that the required devicetree node is always present, satisfying the Kconfig dependency and allowing the driver to be built correctly.

tests/drivers/adc/adc_emul/app.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
&adc0 {
	compatible = "zephyr,adc-emul";
	status = "okay";
	ref-internal-mv = <3300>;
	ref-external1-mv = <5000>;
};
========
/ {
	adc_emul: adc-emul {
		compatible = "zephyr,adc-emul";
		status = "okay";
		ref-internal-mv = <3300>;
		ref-external1-mv = <5000>;
	};
};
